1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
A green CI check answers a narrow question.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Before merging, ask what it tested and which revision it belongs to.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The Community example reviews a delivery change against two requirements.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The thirty-minute assertion passes on both versions. It misses the threshold regression.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The example keeps the successful H1 receipt attached to H1.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The branch moved to H2, so current-head verification stays blocked.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Now run Pro against the synthetic snapshot shipped with the buyer ZIP.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
This command reads the fixture and writes a JSON evidence report locally.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The generated report binds one successful check and flags the stale one.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
A reported pass without a test receipt stays unknown.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The Community release is free on GitHub. Pro is a separate Gumroad download.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Use the report to check evidence. Review behavior and merge decisions separately.
